247
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:39,180
Way to go, guys!

248
00:14:39,560 --> 00:14:41,940
Soon, Tristan will have his body back.

249
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,180
That's awesome!

250
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:46,740
It's a good start, but
this duel's far from over.

251
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,020
Uh, I thought we'd turn
that monkey switch off.

252
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:56,397
So if that's really you
stuck inside there, Tristan,

253
00:14:56,480 --> 00:14:59,697
then why do you keep making all
kinds of weird monkey noises?

254
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:01,637
What do you mean, monkey noises?

255
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:03,360
Oh, no!

256
00:15:03,660 --> 00:15:04,836
I must be going ape!

257
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,177
The longer I stay in here,

258
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:09,657
the more I feel like swinging from
a tree and scratching my armpits!

259
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:11,740
I gotta get my body back!

260
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:15,200
Here we go again, Crump!

261
00:15:15,780 --> 00:15:16,640
Look out!

262
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:18,660
Bingo, baby!

263
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,430
Now!

264
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:23,617
It's time for me to dry
up your ocean, Crump!

265
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:27,480
With yet another card
compliments him is my valentine.

266
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:30,800
Because I activate my
Harpy's Feather Duster.

267
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:36,513
This card sweeps away every magic and
trap card on your side of the field,

268
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:38,604
including your legendary ocean.

269
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:43,840
Now, Cyber Harpy, attack
his legendary fisherman.

270
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:49,080
Aw, yeah.

271
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:50,400
Watch this.

272
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:52,660
Alligator's sword, attack.

273
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:57,260
Catapult Turtles still
has 2,000 defense points.

274
00:15:57,540 --> 00:16:00,440
My attack won't do a thing. Oh, man.

275
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:02,113
Now what am I gonna do?

276
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:07,340
It's still my move, Crump.

277
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:11,537
And I'm not done wiping the field clean
of all your pathetic monsters yet.

278
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:15,760
And my next victim is that
face-down mystery monster of yours.

279
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,940
No, Joey. Don't. It's too risky.

280
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:21,080
Risk is my middle name, Duke.

281
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:22,897
So check this out.

282
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:26,380
Alligator's sword, attack
his face-style monster!

283
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:34,780
You just triggered my Magician
of Faith special effect.

284
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:36,278
Thank you, Wheeler.

285
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:39,640
Now I can bring back one magic card. What?

286
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:42,660
I'll give you one guess
which card I choose.

287
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,580
Time's off. Oh, no.

288
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:46,015
I was afraid of that.

289
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:47,780
A legendary ocean.

290
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:49,400
Sorry about that, Yugi.

291
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:51,880
You fools are making this way too easy.

292
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:54,980
You're defeating yourselves!

293
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:57,760
Calm down, Crump.

294
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:59,380
This duel is still on.

295
00:16:59,620 --> 00:17:01,400
My move, now!

296
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:05,280
Since my Legendary Ocean
Magic card is back in my hand,

297
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:07,440
I can activate it in my next turn.

298
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:11,680
Then I'll play Monster Reborn and
bring back my Legendary Fisherman.

299
00:17:11,860 --> 00:17:13,220
It all adds up.

300
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:17,140
I'll be right back where I was
before, on the road to freedom,

301
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:19,580
with a brand new body to escape in.

302
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:21,997
My chances of success are 99%.

303
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:23,900
All right, Crump.

304
00:17:24,180 --> 00:17:28,700
Now it's about time someone put
you in your place. Go ahead.

305
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:31,220
I'll play Karibo in defense mode.

306
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:36,740
Next, I'll activate card
destruction. Too bad.

307
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:42,320
Now we must throw away all our cards,

308
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:46,600
which means your legendary ocean
card is gone again. Awesome.

309
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:48,780
I knew I could count on you, Yugi.

310
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:55,320
Now, it's time for all of us to
redraw a brand new hand, right, Crump?

311
00:17:57,840 --> 00:17:59,300
I'm through for now.

312
00:17:59,740 --> 00:18:01,520
All right, you brats.

313
00:18:02,340 --> 00:18:03,960
You've done enough, Crump.

314
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:07,121
It's time to lay a little
judgment on these fools.

315
00:18:09,020 --> 00:18:10,960
Crump has been dismissed, kids.

316
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:12,640
They switched again.

317
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:17,097
Those old dudes are passing around
my body like it's going out of style.

318
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:18,340
That's their plan.

319
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:20,384
And that's why they're winning.

320
00:18:20,980 --> 00:18:25,120
You see, this duel is beginning
to take its toll on Yugi and Joey.

321
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:29,085
But the Big Five keep rotating
players to keep themselves fresh.

322
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:30,800
This isn't gonna be easy.

323
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:32,686
Time to bring you to justice.

324
00:18:33,220 --> 00:18:38,120
In case you don't already know, the name's
Johnson, legal expert of the Big Five.

325
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:42,077
And my first order of business is
to clear the field of this penguin,

326
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:43,219
if you don't mind.

327
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:49,220
Meet Judge-Man!

328
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,180
Where are you?

329
00:18:58,820 --> 00:18:59,740
Mokuba!

330
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:02,540
I know you're out there!

331
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:04,100
Can you hear me?

332
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:05,560
Mokuba!

333
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:10,280
Hmm, hear that?

334
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:13,873
It sounds like your so-called
brother is calling for you.

335
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:16,100
Do you want to answer him, Mokuba?

336
00:19:16,660 --> 00:19:17,490
No.

337
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:20,220
Noah is the only brother I have.

338
00:19:24,980 --> 00:19:27,460
This Noah kid is trying my patience.

339
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:30,252
If he has some sort of grudge against me,

340
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:33,237
he should have the guts to
stand up to me face to face.

341
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:37,277
But capturing my defenseless
brother and hiding him in this

342
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:42,120
virtual labyrinth only shows what
a spineless coward Noah really is.

343
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:47,020
Ah, it can't be. That building.

344
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:49,000
It's my design.

345
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:52,597
But I've never shown those
blueprints to anyone.

346
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:54,700
How could Noah have recreated it?

347
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:56,420
Who is this kid?

348
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:12,280
Yo, yo, yo, he's a baby.
